quran[26]{c,v,t}:
  53,1,"By the star when it sets,*"
  53,2,Your guide (i.e. Prophet Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) has never erred nor gone astray.
  53,3,He does not speak out of (his own) desire.
  53,4,It (i.e. his speech) is only a revelation sent down (to him).
  53,5,"The Lord of Mighty Power taught him,"
  53,6,the Lord of absolute perfection. Then He intended to unveil (Himself).
  53,7,And he (Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) was upon the highest horizon (above the Heavens).
  53,8,"Then He (Allah) drew nearer (to Prophet Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) approaching so close,*"
  53,9,until he was only two bows’ length away or nearer.
  53,10,Then He revealed whatever He revealed to His (beloved) servant.
  53,11,The (Prophet’s) heart did not doubt what he saw.
  53,12,Do you then dispute with him about what he saw?
  53,13,"And indeed, he saw Him another time,*"
  53,14,"at the Lote Tree of the Ultimate Boundary (above the seventh heaven),"
  53,15,"by which is the Garden of the Abode,"
  53,16,"while it covered the Lote Tree, whatever (of the Glorious Radiance) covered it."
  53,17,"The (Prophet’s) eye did not turn aside, nor did it exceed the bounds."
  53,18,"Indeed, he saw the greatest of His Lord’s signs (on this night)."
  53,19,"Have you considered (the idols) al-Lat and al-‘Uzza,"
  53,20,"and Manat, the third one (as well)?"
  53,21,(O idolaters!) Are you to have males (i.e. sons) while He females (i.e. daughters)?
  53,22,"(If your estimation is correct,) then this is an unfair distribution!"
  53,23,"These (idols) are only names you have made up—you and your fathers. Allah has not sent down any authority with them. They (the idolators) follow only conjectures and whatever their lower souls desire, although guidance from their Lord has already come to them."
  53,24,Shall every human being have whatever he yearns for?
  53,25,Yet to Allah belong the Hereafter and this world.
  53,26,(Imagine) how many angels are in the heavens whose intercession will be of no benefit (to these idolaters). But (it will become beneficial only) after Allah grants permission to whomever He pleases and approves.
